# sow_allow_reach_witness.rish -- check allowed rooms in the local seed projection.
# The scan names rooms that have tracked inputs yet leave no files or withholding
# record in the projection. Its receipt binds manifest bytes and tracked paths.
# Stale coverage refuses before any missing room is blamed on the projector.
# Content freshness and privacy remain separate whole-projection checks.
#
# tools/s/sow_reach_inputs_witness.rish proves the receipt and refusal transitions
# on small local trees. This witness reads the actual projection when present.
# The roster names seed_projection as its required capability.

say "sow-allow-reach: read the local projection against its coverage inputs"
let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/s/sow_allow_reach_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "sow-allow-reach: the scan refused; read its diagnostic"
assert scan.out contains "empty=0" else "sow-allow-reach: an allowed room has no copied files or withholding record"
assert scan.out contains "withheld_by_design=" else "sow-allow-reach: withholding must be reported"
say "GREEN: sow-allow-reach -- coverage inputs match and absent rooms are accounted for"
